title: "BLF: Lean 4 formalization and computations for Boolean functions that are one bit of a linear form"
authors:
  - family-names: Farland
    given-names: Joseph S.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6809-804X"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jkfarland-bot/BLF"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24466814"
abstract: >-
  A Boolean function is BLF if it is one bit of an integer linear form with a free constant. Lean 4
  proofs, for every n, of the parallelogram inequality for floors of linear forms, that threshold
  functions are BLF and that BLF is closed under XOR with affine functions; and of the exact counts
  4, 16, 208, 10368 for n = 1 to 4 with the structure of BLF(3) and BLF(4). Programs rebuilding the
  counts to n = 6 and the toric chamber counts. Version 1.1 adds Lean proofs of the characterization
  by floor(u) mod 2, the selector lemma for gated thresholds, and that two and three steps of Rule
  110 are not BLF, and programs checking the cellular-automaton constructions. Prepared with Claude (Anthropic). No external human
  referee has reviewed this work.
keywords:
  - Boolean functions
  - threshold functions
  - toric arrangements
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
